# Changes made: .env cleaned

File backend/.env previously contained secrets. On branch fix/security-and-ci it has been replaced with a template placeholder. You MUST set real secrets in your hosting environment.

Example .env (do NOT commit real secrets):

PORT=3000
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=your_db_password
DB_NAME=db_guru_sd
JWT_SECRET=replace_with_strong_random_value
ADMIN_USERNAME=admin

After deploy, consider running:

ADMIN_USERNAME=admin ADMIN_PASSWORD=YourStrongPassword node backend/scripts/seed_admin.js

If backend/.env was previously exposed in commit history, you should remove it from history using the BFG or git filter-repo and then rotate secrets. This repo includes instructions in the PR.
